  "answer": "The study confirmed 2 of the 5 cases it was asked for, so the goal was not met. The two confirmed settings are: 09a95ffa with the lead car 0.5 s later at 0.75x speed (S14), and 12855a41 with the lead car at 0.5x speed (S18). Neither shows the policy rear-ending the lead car. At S14, every run's failure followed the same pattern: the ego braked hard behind the slowed lead car, then drifted left against a RIGHT command and hit a car in the left lane. At S18, the front contacts were flagged 0.5 s after handoff while the ego was still exactly on the recorded path. That looks like a log-replay or bounding-box artifact (the automatic artifact check did not flag it), so S18's confirmation is doubtful. Every other setting failed at most once, or is one to three runs, which is a hint rather than a rate. In this study, no rear-end of the lead car by the policy was shown at 2 Hz.",
